 "text": "Hi, how are you doing these days? A sketch is usually one character, and it' short, often only one scene, kind of like stand up act. A study is a more elaborate thing, usually several scenes and characters, kind of like an episode. Kind of, though studies often have multiple storylines and character changes, so there's more going on than on a sketch show. You can clean them up with layers of masking and gauss blurs, ending each cloud layer with raw window so they still tumble from top to bottom. Your cloud layers look great, but the freshness will only last a few months. Rough paint fades beautifully after a few years, looking much older than it is. Clouds always look like they do from space, thin winter clouds seen on a sunny day.",
